1
00:00:01,049 --> 00:00:02,597
This is ReproDesk.

2
00:00:02,637 --> 00:00:06,513
It captures a bug once, and
gives developers the evidence.

3
00:00:06,553 --> 00:00:08,443
Our demo app is Northwind Gear:

4
00:00:08,483 --> 00:00:11,024
a web shop with two deliberate bugs.

5
00:00:12,067 --> 00:00:16,131
One click on the toolbar icon
arms ReproDesk for this tab only.

6
00:00:16,171 --> 00:00:20,347
Chrome requires that explicit click,
so nothing ever records silently.

7
00:00:20,387 --> 00:00:21,784
Now it is armed.

8
00:00:21,824 --> 00:00:26,081
A rolling buffer keeps only the
last 90 seconds, on this computer.

9
00:00:26,121 --> 00:00:29,860
No keystrokes are collected,
and only this tab is recorded.

10
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,287
Test as usual.

11
00:00:31,327 --> 00:00:34,905
ReproDesk quietly keeps the
latest moments in its buffer.

12
00:00:40,401 --> 00:00:41,818
Something looked wrong?

13
00:00:41,858 --> 00:00:44,622
Save last replay keeps what just happened.

14
00:00:44,662 --> 00:00:48,682
Shortcut: Alt+Shift+R.
No need to reproduce it.

15
00:00:48,722 --> 00:00:51,604
For a known bug, start a Repro Session.

16
00:00:51,644 --> 00:00:56,339
It records the whole path, plus 30
seconds of context from before the start.

17
00:00:56,379 --> 00:00:59,501
Bug 1: the promo code
SUMMER20 shows a discount,

18
00:00:59,541 --> 00:01:01,528
but the total does not change.

19
00:01:01,659 --> 00:01:03,743
Add a marker to flag this moment.

20
00:01:03,783 --> 00:01:06,215
A screenshot is taken automatically.

21
00:01:06,372 --> 00:01:07,936
Now the checkout form.

22
00:01:07,976 --> 00:01:10,472
Typed text is never stored as events.

23
00:01:10,512 --> 00:01:12,627
The video does show pixels, though,

24
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:15,559
so we will hide sensitive
values before sharing.

25
00:01:18,677 --> 00:01:23,220
Bug 2: Place order fails with error E-4021.

26
00:01:26,102 --> 00:01:29,549
If you look at another tab,
recording pauses by itself.

27
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:32,051
Nothing from other tabs is ever stored.

28
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:34,962
Back on the approved tab, capture resumes.

29
00:01:35,002 --> 00:01:38,707
Finish & review stops the
recording and opens the report.

30
00:01:40,581 --> 00:01:43,598
Here is the report: the
video, a live timeline,

31
00:01:43,638 --> 00:01:47,384
and steps drafted from what
really happened. No AI guesses.

32
00:01:47,424 --> 00:01:50,418
Click any row of the timeline
to jump to that moment.

33
00:01:51,625 --> 00:01:54,266
Before sharing, hide sensitive data.

34
00:01:54,306 --> 00:01:58,283
Open a screenshot, blur the
card number, and box the error.

35
00:02:02,846 --> 00:02:05,643
The original screenshot is never modified.

36
00:02:05,683 --> 00:02:08,513
Only the exported copy carries the blur.

37
00:02:09,299 --> 00:02:13,618
Now the video. First, jump to a moment
where the card number is on screen.

38
00:02:13,658 --> 00:02:15,950
Drag a box over the card field.

39
00:02:15,990 --> 00:02:19,855
Blur it from the moment the number
is typed until the error appears.

40
00:02:26,555 --> 00:02:28,812
The error message pushes the form down,

41
00:02:28,852 --> 00:02:32,274
so a second mask covers
the field until the end.

42
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:40,117
The preview shows exactly
what will be exported.

43
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:47,542
Now the card number is hidden in
every frame where it appears.

44
00:02:54,691 --> 00:02:57,586
Describe what happened,
and what you expected.

45
00:02:57,626 --> 00:03:00,525
The expected result is
always written by you.

46
00:03:01,839 --> 00:03:07,759
One click exports an Evidence Package,
an HTML report and a Word document.

47
00:03:09,693 --> 00:03:14,139
The HTML report is self-contained,
with the blurred screenshots,

48
00:03:14,179 --> 00:03:16,631
so developers can open it anywhere.

49
00:03:16,907 --> 00:03:19,949
Everything stays on this
device until you export it.

50
00:03:19,989 --> 00:03:24,730
Administrators can lock settings and restrict
sites with standard browser policies.

51
00:03:24,770 --> 00:03:27,687
ReproDesk: evidence instead of retelling.
